#subtitle: The Republic's place in a Europe sliding toward fascism.

= Foreign Policy

The Foreign Ministry sits with the Radical Party, but the PSOE has real influence over foreign policy from within the coalition. What should our priority be?

@fp_menu

- @league_diplomacy
- @soviet_relations
- @portugal_tension
- @watch_fascism
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@league_diplomacy
title: Pursue collective security through the League of Nations.
on-arrival: west_relation += 2; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 2

Spain has been an active member of the League of Nations since the Republic's founding, briefly holding a non-permanent seat on its Council. Cultivating our standing there - and with France and Britain more broadly - is one of the few levers Madrid has to make its voice heard as the European order comes apart.

@soviet_relations
title: Consider formal diplomatic relations with the Soviet Union.
subtitle: A step no Spanish government has taken since the monarchy fell.

Spain has never established formal diplomatic relations with Moscow - a legacy of the monarchy's anti-Bolshevism that the Republic has, so far, quietly maintained. Opening relations would be a genuine break with that legacy.

- @soviet_yes: Establish relations.
- @soviet_no: Leave the question alone for now.

@soviet_yes
on-arrival: soviet_relation += 3; pce_relation += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation -= 6; ceda_relation -= 10; monarchist_relation -= 5; president_angry += 10

We have established formal diplomatic relations with the Soviet Union. The <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> is pleased, if suspicious of our motives. The CEDA and the monarchist right treat it as confirmation of everything they have always said about the Republic.

@soviet_no

We leave the question alone for now. It is not worth the fight it would provoke.

@portugal_tension
title: Manage tensions with Portugal.
subtitle: Lisbon has hosted General Sanjurjo since his failed 1932 rising, and shows no sign of extraditing him.
on-arrival: monarchist_relation -= 3; izq_rep_relation += 2; coup_progress -= 1 if coup_progress >= 3

We lodge a formal protest with Lisbon over its hosting of Sanjurjo and other monarchist exiles plotting against the Republic. Portugal's own authoritarian government is unmoved, but the protest at least puts the conspirators' foreign patrons on notice.

@watch_fascism
title: Monitor Italian and German support for the monarchist and Falangist right.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if coup_progress < 2 : There is not yet enough evidence of foreign involvement to justify raising this formally. ?]
choose-if: coup_progress >= 2
on-arrival: coup_progress -= 1 if coup_progress >= 2; falange_relation -= 2; monarchist_relation -= 2; izq_rep_relation += 3; west_relation += 1

Our diplomats have quietly confirmed what many suspected: Fascist Italy has been in secret contact with Spanish monarchist plotters for some time, and Nazi Germany watches events in Spain with open interest. Raising this with the League and with Paris and London does not stop the conspiracy, but it puts it on the record, and may complicate matters for the conspirators' foreign patrons if their plans ever come to fruition.
